// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6512 feat: add rule for .NET add-in pipeline host execution (AddInProcess/AddInUtil LOLBins)
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6512
// Pull request author: kosoyyagent
// Change: new rule
// Title: DotNet Add-In Pipeline Host Execution
// Sigma ID: a105eab7-d9b9-4fbe-bf81-21b7e78ed7b5
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: kosoyyagent
// Date: 2026-10-24 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects execution of the Microsoft .NET Framework add-in pipeline host processes
//   (AddInProcess.exe, AddInProcess32.exe). These signed binaries host managed add-in assemblies and
//   can be abused as LOLBins to proxy execution of managed code inside a Microsoft-signed host
//   process. Distinct from AddInUtil.exe (the deployment cache utility), which is covered by its own
//   rules.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate WPF applications that use the .NET add-in framework (MAF). Very uncommon on servers
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Addinprocess/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/180761c491927c04cb946a307acf6ba41e19318b/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_lolbin_addinpipeline.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\AddInProcess.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\AddInProcess32.exe") or (ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName in~ ("AddInProcess.exe", "AddInProcess32.exe"))
